Below are the JSON tool descriptions for each function in the Lodash.chain utility: 

```json
[
    {
        "function": "chain",
        "description": "Initiate the Lodash method chain. Start by wrapping the initial input to enable subsequent method chaining for data manipulation."
    },
    {
        "function": "value",
        "description": "Extract and retrieve the unwrapped value from the Lodash wrapper. This function unwinds the chain and returns the final processed data."
    },
    {
        "function": "filter",
        "description": "Conditionally filter elements within the Lodash wrapper. Provide a predicate function to determine which elements are included or excluded from the result."
    },
    {
        "function": "sortBy",
        "description": "Sort and order the elements in the Lodash wrapper. Specify a property or custom function to define the sorting criteria, allowing for flexible data ordering."
    },
    {
        "function": "map",
        "description": "Apply a method function to each element in the Lodash wrapper, creating a new mapped wrapper. Transform data by modifying each element based on custom logic."
    },
    {
        "function": "reduce",
        "description": "Aggregate the elements in the Lodash wrapper into a single value. Provide a reducer function that accumulates a result, enabling data summarization and complex calculations."
    },
    {
        "function": "find",
        "description": "Locate and return the first element in the Lodash wrapper that satisfies the provided predicate function. Useful for finding specific data points within a collection."
    },
    {
        "function": "size",
        "description": "Determine the size or length of the Lodash wrapper. This function returns an integer representing the count of elements within the wrapped data structure."
    },
    {
        "function": "concat",
        "description": "Concatenate the Lodash wrapper with another array or value, creating a new wrapper. This function enables the combination of data sets for further processing."
    },
    {
        "function": "difference",
        "description": "Compute the difference between the Lodash wrapper and another array, returning a new wrapper with unique elements. Useful for identifying distinct data points."
    },
    {
        "function": "intersect",
        "description": "Find the intersection of the Lodash wrapper with another array, retaining only the common elements. This function helps identify shared data points between two data sets."
    }
]
```

These tool descriptions provide a clear understanding of each function's purpose and how they can be utilized for effective data processing using the Lodash.chain utility.

